<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>How US players are reshaping France and the continent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cc198ea9502b38539ac9ec658309903bb740f0b01bd46eb382685ba4d353ca6</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:33:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260923-how-us-players-are-reshaping-france-and-the-continent" /><summary type="html">In this edition we welcome CNN's correspondent in France, Melissa Bell. Melissa is the author of "Sous l'influence americaine", an investigation into American interference in France and Europe. She tells us about the ways in which American interference is being felt in Europe and France and what we should expect during the 2027 French presidential election campaign.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Trump ramps up his war on the media</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc0d71107cba58dbcb545d272c4a51b20e01bf2f5db464b1492fbc419beebf37</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:25:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260923-trump-ramps-up-his-war-on-the-media" /><summary type="html">US media outlets CNN, Politico and MS NOW are suing the Trump administration after it removed their press credentials and banned them from covering the White House. FRANCE 24 spoke to Steven Herman, executive director of the Jordan Center for Journalism Advocacy and Innovation at the University of Mississippi about the legality of the move and its wider ramnifications.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>UN General Assembly to discuss war, climate and AI</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe380794f7c85d32f9afa1dc963ae1ad172a02a93932e7747739be85cbebad8c</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:20:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260923-un-general-assembly-to-discuss-war-climate-and-ai" /><summary type="html">World leaders are heading to New York for the world's biggest diplomatic gathering: the UN General Assembly. Throughout the week, attention will turn to the war in Iran, climate change and the race to rein in AI. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis and Theresa Squatrito from the London School of Economics discuss what to expect.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>World leaders weigh AI worries, regulations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5f6e0a884a3fd9448931d1bc7ff9159abc6afdb776e6a11263aa1416aa6271f</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:08:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/world-leaders-weigh-ai-worries-regulations" /><summary type="html">AI leaders are due to brief the UN Security Council at an emergency session later today. The meeting comes after weeks of warnings about the potentially uncontrollable risks posed by artificial intelligence. Delano D’Souza reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thomas Chatterton Williams on how Covid-19, George Floyd protests affected US social justice</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88c7e25bc0de323367ad8b5f7d763e47204f5fb0dcaddee4df59db778164ff94</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T12:40:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260923-thomas-chatterton-williams-on-how-covid-19-george-floyd-protests-affected-us-social-justice" /><summary type="html">An acclaimed American author has spoken to FRANCE 24 about his theories on how American society's opinion and ideas of social justice have changed since the presidency of Barack Obama. Thomas Chatterton Williams says the left became disillusioned during Obama's second term, and in later years amid the George Floyd protests and Covid-19 pandemic the discourse shifted – initially for the left, but this also impacted the right. The ripples of those times are still resonating today. His latest book is entitled "Summer of Our Discontent: The Age of Certainty and the Demise of Discourse".</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Chinese beauty products prove resilient amid US-China trade war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1733f990307f7f27c5229f61b749e21c8b605023f39c5c04d47870ca1ff7685</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T12:29:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/chinese-beauty-products-prove-resilient-amid-us-china-trade-war" /><summary type="html">The US-China trade war has hit exports ranging from soybeans to solar panels, but one industry appears to be weathering the tariffs remarkably well. As Donald Trump and Xi Jinping prepare to meet in Washington this week, big-ticket exports are likely to be high on the agenda. But Chinese beauty products such as wigs, hair extensions and false eyelashes have proved highly resilient, with low prices and strong demand encouraging consumers to absorb the extra costs. China’s press-on nail industry, concentrated largely in one city, is also coming through the trade war without a scratch. Bryan Quinn</summary></entry><entry><title>Hurricane Polo churns off Mexico</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:edd5bf732873a144d19e60260757d343d5c808b26cad2117034a5a464057bbb2</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T10:49:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/hurricane-polo-churns-off-mexico" /><summary type="html">Hurricane Polo has strengthened into one of the most powerful Pacific cyclones in decades and is expected to skirt Mexico’s southwestern coast as a Category 5 storm. The Miami-based National Hurricane Center described Polo as an “extremely dangerous” storm, with maximum sustained winds of 165 miles per hour.</summary></entry><entry><title>US President warns Tehran at UN but says talks ongoing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4dfdcf70c4e59e41f80b2c3f1c5e79cd78798be626f930fa7e65e263eeb04e52</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T10:46:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-president-warns-tehran-at-un-but-says-talks-ongoing" /><summary type="html">The day began with Donald Trump threatening to annihilate Iran but ended with a three-hour meeting between US and Iranian mediators, which Trump described as “very good.” Trump also held a high-level meeting with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, with both sides saying they wanted the war in Ukraine to end before winter. Today, as the UN General Assembly continues, Zelensky and Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian are among those expected to address the assembly, as world leaders seek ways to end the two conflicts dominating international politics. France 24 International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Shame': Macron slams Trump's Gaza diplomacy in final UN speech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34cd90ec6a0773ca72add14f0c0d7c05ef0af3738d1ab3d799944c82e0658239</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T10:38:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-shame-macron-slams-trump-s-gaza-diplomacy-in-final-un-speech" /><summary type="html">🇫🇷 French President Emmanuel Macron criticised Gaza diplomacy at the UN General Assembly, calling it a "shameful spectacle" and urging action to reopen humanitarian routes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Live: Syria’s Sharaa vows that Israeli-occupied Golan Heights will remain Syrian</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6547e5d75508b9e09292c6c0f54bf49dbc97a632bcd5f7c0795665fcd12f7ead</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T10:13:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-live-pezeshkian-set-to-address-un-for-the-first-time-since-us-israel-launched-iran-war" /><summary type="html">Syria’s President Ahmed al-Sharaa insisted at the UN Wednesday that the Golan Heights region will remain Syrian after Colombia’s new far-right government last month recognised Israeli sovereignty over the occupied territory. The United Nations considers the strategically important region as Syrian territory under Israeli military occupation. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Cuban delegation walks out during speech of US President</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6bf49a54a2de180abed38033f3d0c59ddc9e21badf855ddaa53ca8c59a7a1ec4</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T09:32:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/cuban-delegation-walks-out-during-speech-of-us-president" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump has once again criticised Cuba, saying in his UN General Assembly address on Tuesday that the country would “fall.” His remarks prompted reactions ranging from outrage to indifference among Cubans, as the island faces one of its most severe economic crises and continues to deal with pressure and threats from its US neighbour. Camille Corcoran reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump and Zelensky discuss path to ending Ukraine war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:470ac4871a96c39d413fd813d3edb313279d4c5bd0468a7a351ac136d2d18bcd</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T09:30:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-and-zelensky-discuss-path-to-ending-ukraine-war" /><summary type="html">On Tuesday, September 22, Donald Trump and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky met in New York to discuss the war in Ukraine. Ahead of Zelensky’s address to the UN General Assembly today, he said he wants the war to end before winter, stressing that people across Ukraine are living in increasingly difficult conditions and that the longer the conflict continues, the greater the risk of further deaths on the frontline. Trump has also said that Ukraine and Russia agreed not to target each other’s energy infrastructure, after previously criticising Kyiv for striking Russian oil refineries. According to France 24 correspondent from Ukraine, Gulliver Cragg, Another potential area for a temporary ceasefire could be the Black Sea, where attacks have disrupted Ukrainian and Russian grain shipments. Ukraine has indicated it is willing to cooperate, although Zelensky has questioned whether Russia would do the same. Analysts say the growing Ukrainian pressure on Russian oil infrastructure could create an opening for a limited ceasefire, although there is uncertainty over how strongly Trump is pushing for such an agreement and when he would want it to happen. France 24 International Affairs editor Philip Turle shares further details.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump media ban sparks solidarity among US news outlets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:738be9e3f0ef2b4c47e9465940b433f61ada86aa41efef59fa73c62df1b4ab5f</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T08:23:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-media-ban-sparks-solidarity-among-us-news-outlets" /><summary type="html">US media outlets are usually fierce competitors, but Donald Trump’s ban on CNN, Politico and MS NOW has prompted an unusual show of solidarity among journalists. The move is changing the way the White House is covered, as Trump arrives in New York for the UN General Assembly. Camille Knight reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>US President Trump threatens "annihilation" of Iran despite successful talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:056fdc31b81b5f80bfc3d1a6ca813ce618330829e5719574e1650f383530fdd8</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T08:22:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-president-trump-threatens-annihilation-of-iran-despite-successful-talks" /><summary type="html">The day began with Donald Trump threatening to annihilate Iran but ended with a three-hour meeting between US and Iranian mediators, which Trump described as “very good.” Trump also held a high-level meeting with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, with both sides saying they wanted the war in Ukraine to end before winter. Today, as the UN General Assembly continues, Zelensky and Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian are among those expected to address the assembly, as world leaders seek ways to end the two conflicts dominating international politics. First, Morgan Ayre reports on the latest developments in the Middle East.</summary></entry><entry><title>Guterres pleads for 'world built on interdependence' in final General Assembly address</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9f7426d890273b5c06341500b89c0d3dd5ff5160872672a8a79feaaabe3c638</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T21:02:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-un-secretary-general-guterres-calls-for-interdependence-in-final-general-assembly-address--e6568de3bc46.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-un-secretary-general-guterres-calls-for-interdependence-in-final-general-assembly-address" /><summary type="html">UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres pleaded for “a world built on interdependence” Tuesday as he made his final address to the annual gathering of world leaders convening to face a formidable menu of challenges, from climate change and war to inequality and the rise of artificial intelligence.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump's world? Leaders navigate consequences of US policy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:edbe213e716b17896384a4140f51d2bb5a4f9cf02a01834fca97f8451c1e5daf</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T18:14:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260922-trump-s-world-leaders-navigate-consequences-of-us-policy--bf2ad7c85eca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260922-trump-s-world-leaders-navigate-consequences-of-us-policy" /><summary type="html">A year ago, Donald Trump went to the rostrum of the United Nations General Assembly and after taking an axe to US aid and development funding, he read the world the riot act. One Iran war later, the US president is sticking to script, with a speech that borrowed much of the language from last year. With citizens on five continents now feeling the pain at the pump, we ask what it will take to tame a global energy crisis whose potential spiral mirrors the contagion of hostilities from the Strait of Hormuz to the mouth of the Red Sea.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Iran, AI and the ICC: Trump makes threats, touts policies at UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:90b3697330f93ef71b6c9d14aafd0f0e3ed383ff199446fc8678b806270c132c</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T17:09:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-iran-ai-and-the-icc-trump-makes-threats-touts-policies-un-general-assembly--12d297e3d635.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-iran-ai-and-the-icc-trump-makes-threats-touts-policies-un-general-assembly" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump launched a full-throated defence of the deeply unpopular US-Israeli war against Iran before the UN General Assembly on Tuesday, claiming that Washington would reach a deal with Tehran after the upcoming US midterm elections. Trump also rejected the idea of global regulation of artificial intelligence, said the government of Cuba would soon "fall", and urged member countries of the International Criminal Court to "resign".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: Trump believes in an agreement after US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59aa2b0b09063e242c49c65f9ecfc019eb2b6cf40f1c655bc915d0f380c7a689</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T16:17:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-iran-trump-believes-in-an-agreement-after-us-midterms--aa11d208ea3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-iran-trump-believes-in-an-agreement-after-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump told the United Nations General Assembly on Tuesday that he would have to decide whether to “annihilate” Iran if Tehran fails to reach a deal to end the war in the Middle East.
 
He added that he believed an agreement was possible after the US midterm elections in November.</summary></entry><entry><title>'UN unable to bring peace to conflicts: We haven’t seen this level of violence in decades’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e409073d2c5e85da97c5bf7417979a6b5f5d3abb1825c2e4f1c4c344f56de579</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:04:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/un-unable-to-bring-peace-to-conflicts-we-haven-t-seen-this-level-of-violence-in-decades--6d0a22913e8c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/un-unable-to-bring-peace-to-conflicts-we-haven-t-seen-this-level-of-violence-in-decades" /><summary type="html">Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi is pleased to welcome Fanny Badache, Researcher at Sciences Po and Lecturer at the University of Geneva. The UN mandate is international peace and security, yet its ability to fulfill that mandate ultimately depends on the cooperation of sovereign states, namely the five powerful permanent members of the Security Council. As the UN is confronted with an increasingly fragmented, volatile and unpredictable international order, Badache argues that when those powers are divided, the mechanisms designed to enable collective security can instead produce paralysis.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump admin's hardline deportation policy an 'attempt to break the global refugee and asylum system'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c58877c94aefe6e920d8089d4e22bc9297d60f935a85cb9602ed37c5b5da7265</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T11:28:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260922-trump-admin-s-hardline-deportation-policy-an-attempt-to-break-the-global-refugee-and-asylum--71f92893b298.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260922-trump-admin-s-hardline-deportation-policy-an-attempt-to-break-the-global-refugee-and-asylum-system" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Washington Post national security reporter Adam Taylor. The Forbidden Stories consortium, involving FRANCE 24 and 25 other media outlets, has spent six months investigating the thousands of people abruptly deported from the United States to third countries, amid concerns over due process and their ability to challenge their removal. The investigation examines how the Trump administration has made deportation a major focus of both US immigration and foreign policy.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Top TV networks – including Fox – revolt in solidarity with media banned by Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9272900c59558a002a6ad26c410fa02c72230efddc8a366385fb26417a47fb4b</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T10:59:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-top-tv-networks-_-including-fox-_-revolt-in-solidarity-with-media-banned-by-trump--37c5ae261fb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-top-tv-networks-%E2%80%93-including-fox-%E2%80%93-revolt-in-solidarity-with-media-banned-by-trump" /><summary type="html">The top five US television networks staged a revolt on Monday when they effectively boycotted coverage of President Donald Trump to protest his decision to ban three news outlets from the White House. "No administration should restrict a news organization because it objects to its reporting," ABC, CBS, CNN, Fox and NBC said in a joint statement.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump: US outlets boycott Trump over media ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8366a14ce103426a990fc392a114ada503f8ea64a7913bbd79f4313506fe096</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T10:53:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-donald-trump-us-outlets-boycott-trump-over-media-ban--ed4501795fdd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-donald-trump-us-outlets-boycott-trump-over-media-ban" /><summary type="html">During a ribbon-cutting ceremony for a new helipad at the White House on Monday, Donald Trump made a brief statement that was inaudible.
 
In response to Trump’s decision to bar MS NOW, CNN and Politico from the White House, US television networks, including ABC, CBS, NBC and Fox News, suspended their pooled coverage of the president.</summary></entry><entry><title>'No peace without justice,' Macron tells UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d4242518315ea23b5e0e2ac09e6b216b7ef0532b12360f847712044d8247f0c</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T10:09:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-live-guterres-to-open-un-general-assembly-in-final-speech-of-his-mandate--57a3ef49f3db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-live-guterres-to-open-un-general-assembly-in-final-speech-of-his-mandate" /><summary type="html">UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres opened the General Assembly in New York on Tuesday for the last time before his term ends on December 31. Guterres was followed at the podium by Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, US President Donald Trump and French President Emmanuel Macron. Read our liveblog for highlights and replays of their addresses.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>World leaders gather at UN amid wars, AI fears and global divisions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:778747701887d4933ee4e9eac3e95531b6001ec77ab923b0941e7b210be9a95a</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T03:49:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-world-leaders-gather-at-un-amid-wars-ai-fears-and-global-divisions--d1ee36515d6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-world-leaders-gather-at-un-amid-wars-ai-fears-and-global-divisions" /><summary type="html">World leaders are gathering at the United Nations this week against a backdrop of wars in the Middle East and Ukraine, rising fears over artificial intelligence and mounting economic and climate pressures. The annual General Assembly will test whether the 193-member body can still bring countries together to tackle crises that increasingly transcend borders.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US, Denmark and Greenland sign security deal to bolster Arctic security</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:308e8418fa69a7478bca6c99f9a9a94fd3b49df3a2e6bf1e25a6bde2868010c4</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T23:30:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-us-denmark-and-greenland-to-sign-security-deal-on-tuesday--e3730ada4f03.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-us-denmark-and-greenland-to-sign-security-deal-on-tuesday" /><summary type="html">The United States, Denmark and Greenland on Tuesday signed a security agreement expanding US involvement in Greenland’s defence while affirming Danish sovereignty over the Arctic territory.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Paramount settles with US states, clearing path for Warner Bros. merger</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8ca34573cd976217c9eda3e00a1c08849dcf8f2c67e845aa45c54694263cd28</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T22:48:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-paramount-settles-with-us-states-clearing-path-for-warner-bros-merger--f9c2a041c5b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-paramount-settles-with-us-states-clearing-path-for-warner-bros-merger" /><summary type="html">Paramount has reached a settlement with California and 11 other states that clears a major legal hurdle to its $110 billion takeover of Warner Bros. Discovery, with the deal imposing commitments on film production, jobs and editorial independence at CNN and CBS News.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Ed Sheeran hit by viral false claims after Macklemore controversy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f644f299b949950a221babf755ac9cc24c125a8c6cf067b2addf8ad22fc30a1d</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T21:05:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ed-sheeran-hit-by-viral-false-claims-after-macklemore-controversy-1--cd1d21c7e597.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ed-sheeran-hit-by-viral-false-claims-after-macklemore-controversy-1" /><summary type="html">Ed Sheeran's controversial US tour has sparked a wave of viral rumours. A false claim that his music was removed from Spotify racked up more than 3 million views on X, despite his music remaining available. Another video, viewed over 14 million times, falsely suggested Sheeran was now defiantly performing solo after all his support acts withdrew. But not only is the footage dated, Sheeran has in fact replaced the backing musicians. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>'Banking on a national brand': Bolsonaro sons Carlos, Jair Renan run for power in Brazil's south</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aac486af8f8bd5fc41b62b97223bf176fe93d0e36c5c309777027c08077411f5</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T17:46:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-bolsonaro-sons-carlos-and-race-for-power-brazil-south--3d3858e0bb77.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-bolsonaro-sons-carlos-and-race-for-power-brazil-south" /><summary type="html">Flavio Bolsonaro is not the only member of his family campaigning in his father’s shadow. The former president's eldest son, who is now polling neck and neck with incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, can count on two of his brothers, who are standing in the senatorial and legislative elections. In Santa Catarina, one of Brazil’s most pro-Bolsonaro southern states, their surname alone is enough to secure victory.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>CNN, MS NOW, Politico to sue Trump administration after White House ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3f0b8d845c3011de1a6d7473f8b3726cb6469d9904468d5658cde5102042c74</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T14:34:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-cnn-ms-now-politico-sue-trump-administration-after-white-house-ban--1eae5b26a76f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-cnn-ms-now-politico-sue-trump-administration-after-white-house-ban" /><summary type="html">US media outlets CNN, MS NOW and Politico announced Monday they were filing suit after US President Donald Trump banned their journalists from the White House last week. The ban on the three outlets marks an escalation in the Trump administration's years-long assault on the country's press freedoms.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Midterm elections: Trump looms large over 2026 vote as Democrats eye gains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ee8b42d04a912f2b93d69cdbb00da8a690f756caedd63f2b305ceef28b04512</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T12:51:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/midterm-elections-trump-looms-large-over-2026-vote-as-democrats-eye-gains--8893a9a014d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/midterm-elections-trump-looms-large-over-2026-vote-as-democrats-eye-gains" /><summary type="html">With the US midterm elections now just six weeks away, we’ll speak to our Washington correspondent Fraser Jackson about whether President Donald Trump could help or hurt his party’s chances. Polls have pointed to what some are calling a “blue wave”, with Democrats potentially regaining control of the House, while the Senate race remains more uncertain. Trump has ramped up campaigning, including spending heavily on advertising and proposing $5,000 payments to voters who support Republicans. But with his approval ratings under pressure amid the war in Iran and the Middle East, and rising oil, gasoline and commodity prices compared with before he took office, the political landscape could still shift significantly in the coming weeks.</summary></entry></feed>
